Executive Summary
This project restores and commissions a Festo automation trainer as a functioning industrial automation cell while providing a structured learning experience in pneumatics, sensors, electrical interfaces, PLC programming, system integration, commissioning, documentation, and troubleshooting.
The automation cell moves parts through a magazine and conveyor, identifies material using inductive inspection, makes a diverter decision, feeds acceptable parts to a stacker, performs pick-and-place operations, and ejects the completed assembly.
The project is organized into seven engineering phases. Each phase has defined goals, learning requirements, responsibilities, deliverables, evidence, and exit criteria. Leadership is shared so that both students participate in the major technical disciplines.
