1. Project Overview
The restoration project is built around five major machine functions: magazine feeding, conveyor transport, part rejection, stacking, and final assembly discharge.
Subsystem	Primary Function
Magazine	Feeds parts into the automation sequence.
Conveyor	Transfers parts between processing stations.
Part Rejection	Uses inspection results to divert parts when required.
Stacker	Feeds, picks, and stacks parts into an assembly.
Final Assembly Discharge	Ejects the completed assembly and resets the cycle.

